Prayer is a means of last resort, it's much better to avoid using it
up unnecessarily.

"Not being hit" is generally a good idea, and works equally well to
avoid the need for MC3 or displacement.  Of course things like
Elbereth that help you not get hit are partially counteracted by
displacement (e.g. the case explained in monmove.c at line 251).

Personally, from the later early game on I prefer MC3 over
displacement because it's a better defense for me against carelessness/
laziness (my two leading causes of death).  In the very early game I
prefer displacement by a small margin.

At any rate, a non-elven ranger generally has no problem trading
displacement for MC3 by the time I'd want to, so starting with the
cloak of displacement is a definite advantage IMO.  It's not a big
enough advantage to overcome the elven bow+arrows advantage, IMO, but
that's a fairly close call that I could go either way on.


